WEBVTT

00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:04.940
Wait!

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:06.660
This way!

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:09.900
Darn it...

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.490
Being slow is a huge disadvantage 
at times like these.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:16.950
And since it's such a tight 
space, I can't call Syrup.

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.200
This way!

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.310
I hope you're read—

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:30.840
What is this?! A slime?!

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.750
Well? Think you can climb up?

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:35.960
If you can catch us, we'll give you a reward!

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:40.520
Oh, I know!

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:42.250
[Psychokinesis]!

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:48.480
Surprised?

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.440
[Psychokinesis] lets me move other 
objects at will, even monsters!

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.100
[Venom Capsule]!

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.700
And also...

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:01.580
What's going on?!

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.300
That made it a little 
harder to move, didn't it?

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:08.430
And to make extra sure... 
Slime, if you would!

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:12.030
Okay, I'll be going now.

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.190
What's wrong? Why'd you freeze up?

00:01:16.970 --> 00:01:20.650
Oh n-no, w-we've been c-c-caught.

00:01:21.260 --> 00:01:23.850
W-W-We sure are c-c-c-c-caught.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.080
<i>Let's play again sometime!</i>

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.490
Wh-What was that all about?

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.580
Yes! This is the stuff Sally was looking for!

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:36.350
Acquired [Feet of the Dead]. 
Acquired [Hands of Salvation]. 
Acquired [Ghost Girl's Clothes].

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.350
And, uh... what's this?

00:01:36.350 --> 00:01:38.860
<i>"Ghost Girl's Clothes"?</i>

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:41.810
Maple again?!

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:45.080
We can have stuff in our game that <i>seems</i> 
bugged, but we can't have actual bugs!

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:48.540
I can't believe they froze.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.610
I guess having the poison, the 
slime, and the items there

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.830
all at once surpassed 
the game's object limit?

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:59.140
Why'd you put a slime at the 
bottom of a pitfall, anyway?!

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:03.380
It seemed like a good idea at the time...

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.140
We can talk later.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.080
I believe fixing the bug 
quickly is more important.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:11.160
Uh, yeah... You're right. 
You're exactly right.

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:15.400
I don't think any other player 
would've done that, though.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.610
A bug is a bug. We cannot 
allow it to persist.

00:02:18.860 --> 00:02:22.170
A-All right, everyone! Start 
working on a fix! Now!

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:23.240
Right!

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.000
My stomach hurts...

00:02:27.350 --> 00:02:36.130
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:56.000
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:04:01.360
<b>Maxing Defense </b>and <b>the Seventh Event</b>.

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:06.760
Sally, sorry to call you 
here on such short notice.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.460
It's okay... What's that you're wearing?

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:12.360
It comes with a skill called [Poltergeist]

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:15.540
that lets you move up to ten 
objects around at the same time!

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.430
I was looking for those items to give 
to you, and this came with them.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.390
Items to give to me?

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.760
Yeah!

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:25.170
Here.

00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:26.780
Oh, aren't those...

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:28.610
These are what you wanted, right?

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:32.420
Since you can't explore 
Level 6, I got them for you.

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:36.500
Thanks, Maple! I'm gonna 
try them out right now!

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.920
Sorry, Maple!

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.090
I couldn't use this one.

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:44.330
Huh? Why not?

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.210
Try equipping it in the field.

00:04:46.210 --> 00:04:48.830
I'll be off grinding for levels somewhere.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.930
See ya!

00:04:53.730 --> 00:04:57.160
Is it that hard to use?

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.620
[Hands of Salvation]!

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:03.960
Oh... Yeah, I can see why 
Sally can't use this.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:05.140
So much for that.

00:05:05.660 --> 00:05:07.210
Huh? Oh, it's Mii.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:12.570
Sorry! Were you waiting long?

00:05:12.570 --> 00:05:16.260
No problem. But was it okay to call 
you here on such short notice?

00:05:16.260 --> 00:05:18.750
Sure! I didn't have any plans today.

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:20.090
Thanks!

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:23.460
To get right down to business... could 
you help me defeat this monster?

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.930
Sure! I did promise you, after all!

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.890
Hm, graves...

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.630
There are supposed to be 
hitodama monsters around here

00:05:32.630 --> 00:05:36.040
that grant a skill you can use to 
strengthen flames when you defeat them.

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:39.360
But they use AoE attacks, 
and they're pretty strong.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.970
You can leave that to me, then!

00:05:41.970 --> 00:05:44.790
[Loving Sacrifice]! 
[Throne of the Heavenly King]!

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:51.850
Now we'll always be safe.

00:05:51.850 --> 00:05:55.310
Just don't stray too far from 
me, 'cause I can't move.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.660
Uh... Okay, got it.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:04.920
[Flame]!

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:11.760
Huh?! Even your [Flame] can't beat them?

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.100
I just don't have enough firepower...

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.570
Don't worry!

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:27.960
As long as I stay on this throne, 
you shouldn't take damage.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:31.490
Nice! Now I can take the 
time to do my incantation.

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:38.200
O crimson glow that doth banish 
the blackest darkness...

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.360
Vein of burning heat coursing 
betwixt destruction and chaos,

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:46.300
I summon thy power here in accordance 
with the eternal contract.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:51.760
With thy violent breath that spilleth 
from fractures in the world,

00:06:51.760 --> 00:06:54.850
make the earth tremble, fill the heavens,

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:57.430
and eradicate all enemies before me!

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:59.960
[Volcano Explosion]!

00:07:09.150 --> 00:07:12.110
Whoa! That's so cool!

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.520
That was amazing!

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:19.710
I shouldn't be surprised you 
can use a skill like that!

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:21.690
Thanks.

00:07:21.690 --> 00:07:24.980
Oh, hey! Since we're together, 
wanna hit up a café?

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:26.830
I know a really good one!

00:07:27.570 --> 00:07:31.800
You seem like you know more about stuff 
like that than about the battlefield.

00:07:31.800 --> 00:07:33.800
Yeah, maybe.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:38.720
What's Sally doing today?

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:42.920
Sally can't deal with the kind 
of atmosphere Level 6 has,

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:45.990
so she's just been grinding 
in Level 5 all day.

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:48.730
Really? That's kind of surprising.

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:51.870
She seemed like the flawless 
type that could handle anything.

00:07:51.870 --> 00:07:54.700
Since we can't play together 
as much right now,

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:58.140
we've promised to pair up in the next event.

00:07:58.140 --> 00:08:00.700
You're such good friends. I envy you.

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.350
We're together all the 
time in real life, too.

00:08:06.180 --> 00:08:09.420
Don't you ever go exploring 
with the others in your guild?

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:14.430
Hmm... I do, but I feel more 
at ease when I'm with you.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:17.550
Oh, because you have to 
be the leader with them?

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:20.430
If I'd known it would be like this,

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:23.230
I never would've created 
this kind of character.

00:08:24.260 --> 00:08:26.540
Aw, you really do have it rough.

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.020
It <i>is</i> rough.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.870
I was a fool to get all 
cocky and put on this act

00:08:30.870 --> 00:08:35.360
just because I got some cool skills.

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.330
Well, then, just give me a call anytime!

00:08:38.330 --> 00:08:40.120
You know, when you need a breather!

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.890
Okay, if you don't mind...

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.210
Oh, it's Maple and Mii.

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.170
Heya!

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:49.230
Well, this is quite the unusual pairing.

00:08:49.230 --> 00:08:50.380
I-Indeed.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:53.050
You two are a pretty unusual 
pairing yourselves!

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:57.270
I went to your guild to challenge 
Sally to a duel, and she wasn't there.

00:08:57.270 --> 00:09:00.420
I forgot she has a problem with ghosts.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:03.420
So I took it upon myself to duel her instead.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:06.140
I beat her at her own game and cut her down.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:11.130
And then Mii just razed 
everything to the ground!

00:09:11.130 --> 00:09:13.240
Her fire was so pretty!

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:15.680
I have progressed with my training, as well.

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.750
I've gained even more powerful 
magic and skills, after all.

00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.710
Oh, uh... Yeah, that's right!

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:24.490
I gotta get revenge on 
you sometime, too, Maple.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:27.370
The last time we fought was during 
that one event, and you clobbered me.

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:29.500
Hey! I'm not gonna lose, either!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:31.090
I'm growing fast!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.590
Well, you know who else is growing?

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:34.290
Payne.

00:09:34.290 --> 00:09:37.160
Wouldn't it make more sense to say "me"?!

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:42.990
I'd like to, but no matter how many 
times I fight Sally, I can't beat her.

00:09:42.990 --> 00:09:45.620
You'll never have a chance 
at beating Sally or Maple

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:47.800
if you can't even beat me.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:51.110
Don't worry, we'll win the 
next guild competition!

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:52.980
That's what you're thinking 
too, isn't it, Mii?

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:54.120
It is.

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:57.150
As the guildmaster of Flame Emperors,

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.450
I can't simply sit back and accept a loss.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:01.050
Challenge accepted!

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:04.660
Oh, but... I'd appreciate it if 
you didn't use piercing attacks.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:07.480
But we can't win without those!

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:15.350
I've been looking for a tame monster like 
your turtle that I can keep with me.

00:10:15.350 --> 00:10:19.560
I figured there would be some 
ghost-type ones in Level 6, but...

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:23.430
Oh, if you find one, don't 
use it against Sally!

00:10:24.680 --> 00:10:25.020
Busted, huh?

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:28.640
If you do, I'll come take a bite out 
of you in the next guild competition!

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:29.770
Chomp, chomp!

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:34.110
I'd rather you didn't do that, I think.

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:35.460
Anyway...

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:38.910
Guess I'm gonna head out 
now. You staying, Kasumi?

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:42.610
No, I was just thinking 
of logging out myself.

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.420
See you, Maple, Mii.

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:44.990
Right.

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:45.880
See ya.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:47.220
Bye!

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:53.030
That was close!

00:10:53.030 --> 00:10:56.090
They showed up out of nowhere, 
and my guard was down.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:01.260
Next time, we'll get our tea at a place 
our friends are less likely to come to.

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.370
Thanks. I'd appreciate that.

00:11:07.410 --> 00:11:08.810
Rawr!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.730
I'd like to thank all of 
you for being here today!

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:15.940
We will now begin the seventh event!

00:11:15.940 --> 00:11:19.490
The playing fields will be 
divided up by difficulty level,

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:22.470
Difficulty: Beginner

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:22.340
Difficulty: Intermediate

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:22.470
Difficulty: Climax

00:11:17.300 --> 00:11:22.230
Difficulty: Ultimate

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:21.740
so you can choose where you want to go.

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:19.850
Difficulty: Beginner

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:20.140
Difficulty: Intermediate

00:11:20.150 --> 00:11:20.430
Difficulty: Climax

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:20.730
Difficulty: Ultimate

00:11:20.740 --> 00:11:20.980
Difficulty: Beginner

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:21.390
Difficulty: Beginner

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:21.810
Difficulty: Beginner

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:24.850
Each party will have their very own map,

00:11:24.850 --> 00:11:27.710
so you'll never clash with any other parties.

00:11:27.710 --> 00:11:30.340
You can let loose as much as you want!

00:11:30.340 --> 00:11:33.020
The event will last five real-life days.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:35.340
You can log out when you 
need to during that time,

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:39.670
If you complete the event, medals will be 
awarded depending on your difficulty level.

00:11:35.480 --> 00:11:39.670
Difficulty: 
Climax

00:11:35.650 --> 00:11:39.670
Difficulty: Intermediate

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:39.670
Difficulty: Beginner

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:39.670
Difficulty: Ultimate

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.670
Completion Reward

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.670
Completion Reward

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.670
Completion Reward

00:11:36.110 --> 00:11:39.670
Completion Reward

00:11:39.670 --> 00:11:42.590
And now to begin the countdown!

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.800
It's been a long time since 
we last saw you, Sally.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:46.900
I'm keeping Sally all to myself this time!

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:47.470
Ten! Nine! Eight!

00:11:46.900 --> 00:11:49.240
It's been so long since we played as a duo!

00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:51.630
Seven! Six! Five! Four!

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:51.630
We want the highest difficulty level, right?

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:54.530
Three! Two! One!

00:11:51.630 --> 00:11:54.530
Of course! I'm raring to go!

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:55.570
Zero!

00:11:55.570 --> 00:11:57.880
Off you go!

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:12.370
So we're supposed to work our way up that?

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.830
Looks like it has ten floors total.

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:18.260
We could get transported somewhere 
else partway up, though.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.740
Ooh! Beating this would feel so rewarding!

00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:23.090
All right, let's get moving.

00:12:29.570 --> 00:12:32.120
Looks like the first floor 
is a regular dungeon.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:34.620
We'd better be careful not 
to bump into anything.

00:12:34.620 --> 00:12:36.980
Okay, then... [Loving Sacrifice]!

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:38.820
And then [Wooly]!

00:12:45.350 --> 00:12:48.500
I-Is this how dungeon-exploring 
usually works?

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:51.450
This way, we won't fall into any pitfalls,

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.290
plus our defense is boosted. 
Two birds with one stone!

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.170
Maple! There's a monster!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.830
[Deploy Armaments]!

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:02.980
Got it!

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:06.870
You sure did, but... that's some 
look you're sporting right now.

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:13.580
Sally...

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:16.060
Yeah. I think it's coming up from below.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:17.380
[Wool Hunting]!

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:23.630
Maple, isn't your [Deploy Armaments]...

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.240
Oh, yeah! It's [Machine God V2]!

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.990
Apparently it'll change 
form however I want it to.

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:34.660
I mean, not that anything 
surprises me anymore, but...

00:13:42.070 --> 00:13:43.130
Maple, back me up!

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.780
[Commence Attack]!

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.390
[Super Speed]!

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:50.100
Sorry, Sally!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.560
Nah, it's all good!

00:13:52.760 --> 00:13:54.040
[Cover Move]!

00:13:58.730 --> 00:14:00.070
Something's coming!

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:02.820
[Pierce Guard]!

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:09.320
Maple, attack the inside of its mouth!

00:14:09.320 --> 00:14:10.170
Its mouth?!

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:11.380
When it uses its breath.

00:14:11.380 --> 00:14:14.950
If it repels attacks from outside, its 
insides are probably its weakness!

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.660
Oh, yeah! Got it!

00:14:25.260 --> 00:14:26.170
Maple?!

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:28.190
[Commence Attack]!

00:14:32.510 --> 00:14:34.970
All right! First floor cleared!

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.180
She got us again!

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:41.360
Wasn't the whole point of that 
dragon its high defensive power?!

00:14:41.360 --> 00:14:44.170
That's how it was designed...

00:14:44.170 --> 00:14:46.430
But if it was <i>too</i> strong, it'd be unbeatable,

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:48.430
so we made the inside of 
the mouth its weakness,

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:51.980
and created an opening to take advantage 
of that when it uses its breath.

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:55.800
We did set its HP pretty high, too...

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:59.890
Never thought anyone would jump 
right into its mouth, though.

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:02.220
Maple is exactly the type to do just that.

00:15:02.220 --> 00:15:03.710
We should have foreseen it.

00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:09.110
B-But remember, they're still 
only on the first floor!

00:15:09.110 --> 00:15:10.390
Yeah, exactly!

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:14.360
The first floor <i>should</i> be 
the easiest one to get past!

00:15:14.360 --> 00:15:17.480
Yeah, and the monster on the 
second floor is even tougher!

00:15:17.480 --> 00:15:20.690
And I'll bet it's the kind of monster 
that Maple has the most trouble with.

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:24.880
Yeah! Even Maple won't be able 
to get past that one easily!

00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:27.150
I see. I look forward to seeing it.

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:34.340
The second floor's a library, huh?

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:40.910
Wait, why are you wearing glasses?

00:15:40.910 --> 00:15:42.750
I bought them at the shop earlier.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.660
What do you think? Do I look smart?

00:15:44.660 --> 00:15:46.650
Maybe if you hadn't just asked me that...

00:15:49.340 --> 00:15:50.440
Maple, something's coming!

00:15:50.440 --> 00:15:51.300
Okay!

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:02.730
[Commence Attack]!

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:13.380
Huh?! What is this?!

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:14.200
Maple!

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:15.280
Huh?!

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.270
That's [Machine God]!

00:16:19.270 --> 00:16:21.330
Wait, you mean it took your skill?!

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:25.010
[Web User]!

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:32.870
[Ice Pillar]!

00:16:37.510 --> 00:16:40.350
Maple, did it take any other skills from you?

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.120
[Seeping Chaos], 
[Throne of the Heavenly King],

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
<b>Cover Move IV</b>

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
<b>Provocation Cover</b>

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
<b>Hydra Eater</b>

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
Provocation

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
Draws monsters' attention to a certain area. Cooldown is three minutes.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
Conditions for Acquisition

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
Draw the attention of ten monsters at once.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:46.310
Items can be used.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:45.920
[Pandemonium], [Predator], [Atrocity]...

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.280
They're almost all gone!

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:51.550
All I have left are 
[Provocation] and... uh...

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:54.240
So that thing's practically 
a pseudo-Maple now?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.660
Maple, what's your VIT right now?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:00.620
Uh, it's... a little over 2,000.

00:17:00.620 --> 00:17:03.140
2,000? Uh...

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:06.690
Then you should be able to withstand 
its attacks for a little while.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:09.270
My ice pillars can't be 
destroyed, so just stay here.

00:17:09.270 --> 00:17:12.610
And if you could take about half 
the targets, that'd be great.

00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:13.590
Got it!

00:17:23.990 --> 00:17:25.140
[Provocation]!

00:17:28.690 --> 00:17:30.420
[A Step Toward the Underworld]!

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.050
[Fireball]!

00:17:40.980 --> 00:17:43.680
[Loving Sacrifice]! That's 
what I was waiting for!

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:45.160
[Fireball]!

00:17:45.160 --> 00:17:50.140
Oh, right! [Loving Sacrifice] takes 
in damage directed at allies!

00:17:52.130 --> 00:17:53.470
[Double Slash]!

00:18:09.310 --> 00:18:12.440
Thanks! There are more targets now!

00:18:12.850 --> 00:18:14.030
[Provocation]!

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:19.690
Huh?

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:33.840
Maple!

00:18:36.100 --> 00:18:38.550
It's okay! I didn't take any damage!

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:40.530
Whoa!

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:45.220
Wow... They even fleshed out 
the inside of this thing.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:47.930
Maple, hang in there for a little bit, okay?

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:49.730
I'll take care of this in no time!

00:18:58.040 --> 00:18:59.330
<i>I guess I'll try it...</i>

00:18:59.790 --> 00:19:04.050
Hmm, what should I do? 
Eat it like I usually do?

00:19:04.050 --> 00:19:05.820
It's paper, though...

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:06.980
Huh?

00:19:17.000 --> 00:19:18.980
I-I'm beat.

00:19:20.580 --> 00:19:21.490
<i>But...</i>

00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:23.640
<i>I got to test out some things.</i>

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.930
Sally!

00:19:29.170 --> 00:19:30.790
You beat it already?

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:32.780
That's amazing! You were so quick!

00:19:32.780 --> 00:19:34.230
Oh... Yeah.

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:37.300
I guess I managed thanks 
to the shoes you gave me.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:40.110
Anyway, did you get your skills back?

00:19:40.110 --> 00:19:43.070
Yeah, we're good! They're 
all back the way they were!

00:19:43.070 --> 00:19:45.980
Thank goodness! Welcome back, guys!

00:19:44.970 --> 00:19:45.980
Good.

00:19:46.280 --> 00:19:48.240
Secretary

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.240
They made it through.

00:19:48.240 --> 00:19:49.620
Y-Yeah...

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:52.430
B-But it did keep Maple quiet!

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:55.350
It really was a sort of monster 
she'd have trouble with!

00:19:55.670 --> 00:19:59.130
It seems that was not the 
case for Sally, though.

00:20:00.220 --> 00:20:02.010
We'll get her next time!

00:20:08.990 --> 00:20:12.050
The third floor looks totally 
different from the others, too.

00:20:12.050 --> 00:20:14.600
Are we gonna get jumped by a 
boss right off the bat again?

00:20:18.060 --> 00:20:21.260
I guess the ground itself deals fixed damage?

00:20:21.260 --> 00:20:25.210
You might be fine with your high 
defense, but I'd better be careful.

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:35.460
That looks super strong!

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:39.090
[Ice Pillar]!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:42.760
[Web User]!

00:20:46.010 --> 00:20:47.680
[A Step Toward the Underworld]!

00:20:47.680 --> 00:20:49.220
[Ancient Sea]!

00:20:51.480 --> 00:20:53.100
[Water Ball]!

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.140
It didn't work?

00:20:58.140 --> 00:21:00.440
Well, then... Syrup! [Spirit Cannon]!

00:21:00.800 --> 00:21:03.980
Turtle!

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:06.190
Looks like that attack might work!

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:08.180
Wait, what?! Hang on a minute!

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:09.370
It's changing forms?!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:13.210
What is this? It doesn't feel cold, but...

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:15.190
It'll probably give us a status abnormality.

00:21:15.190 --> 00:21:16.960
We have to finish it before we freeze!

00:21:18.920 --> 00:21:20.880
Okay! [Atrocity]!

00:21:36.690 --> 00:21:37.750
Weak!

00:21:40.610 --> 00:21:42.730
They got us <i>again</i>!

00:21:42.730 --> 00:21:45.500
No, I believe that was quite 
a difficult fight for them.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.590
Y-You really think so?

00:21:47.590 --> 00:21:48.820
How do you figure?

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:52.040
Secretary

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:52.040
We landed a hit on Maple, did we not?

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:53.630
With terrain damage.

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:01.310
Just the terrain?

